# Trusted integration workers

Reuse `roboflow_workflows.utils.subprocess_supervisor.run_in_subprocess` for
trusted Python integration workers. The module name must be application-owned,
never supplied by a Workflow. Pass an absolute monotonic deadline, bounded JSON
inputs and a result-validation callback. The callback runs before temporary
files are removed and must validate schema, file type, sizes and allocation
bounds before loading results. It must check the deadline between bounded work.

Keep destination validation, connector policy, remote cancellation and result
semantics in the integration. The supervisor owns request serialization, process
launch, terminate/kill/reap, bounded error reports and temporary cleanup. Secrets
travel over stdin, never argv; supply them for error redaction too.

This is process isolation for trusted code, not an OS sandbox, a hard RSS cap,
or proof of remote query cancellation. Only the direct child is terminated.
Workers that spawn descendants require an explicit process-group/job policy.
Allow for the documented cleanup interval after the request deadline and size
memory and temporary storage for concurrent workers.

Test success, launch failure, timeout, a child ignoring termination, cleanup
after invalid results, bounded requests and errors, and integration-specific
result validation. Verify that connector hooks never affect the parent.
